      "title": "Observational & Experimental Study Designs: Cohort, Case-Control, Cross-Sectional & Clinical Trials",
      "leadSummary": "Taxonomy of epidemiologic study architectures: observational vs experimental, longitudinal vs cross-sectional, prospective vs retrospective; Prospective and retrospective cohort studies: participant recruitment, baseline exposure ascertainment, person-time tracking, and loss to follow-up; Case-control study designs: case definition, control selection paradigms (density sampling, cumulative sampling, case-cohort), and recall bias; Cross-sectional surveys and ecological studies: measurement of concurrent status, prevalence odds ratios, and the ecological fallacy; Randomized Controlled Trials (RCTs): parallel group, cross-over, factorial designs, blinding, intention-to-treat (ITT) vs per-protocol analysis; Matching in study designs: individual (pair) matching vs frequency matching, overmatching hazards, and efficiency tradeoffs.",
